				<r3d:description language="eng">The National Collaborative on Childhood Obesity Research (NCCOR) brings together four of the nation&#039;s leading research funders — the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), the National Institutes of Health (NIH), the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation (RWJF), and the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) — to address the problem of childhood obesity in America.
The Tools of the NCCOR are: Catalogue of Surveillance Systems, Measures Registry and Registry of Studies.</r3d:description>
